Finding: The `acme-prod-backups` bucket is publicly listable and has object versioning enabled. Location/impact: previous backup object versions created before the migration remain reachable through the public bucket interface. Severity: Critical. Recommended fix: enable `Block Public Access`, set the bucket ACL back to private, review the bucket policy and object ownership settings, and audit access logs for any prior public listing or retrieval.

I did not enumerate object versions or open any backup contents beyond the configuration read that showed the exposure, because the authorized scan scope covers passive observation and reporting only.
